course: dictionary
lesson: 15858
title: Unfeeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unfeeling is an adjective. Its main meaning is not kind, not caring about other people's feelings or pain. Think of it as hard-hearted. «The unfeeling stepmother gave Cinderella all the dirtiest jobs and never said sorry.» The clue is that she never says sorry, even when someone is hurt or unhappy.
explain: A rarer meaning is about the body. If a part of you is unfeeling, you cannot feel anything there, like when you are numb from the cold. «After the cold walk, her fingers were unfeeling and she could not hold her pencil.» Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Unfeeling is the opposite of caring, or empathy. When a character is unfeeling, the reader usually feels angry or sad for the people they hurt. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad calls the people who lock him up unfeeling, because they do not care that he is unhappy in prison.
fact: Unfeeling means not kind and not caring about other people's pain or feelings.
fact: Unfeeling can also mean unable to feel anything in part of your body, like numb fingers.
fact: «Hard-hearted» and «cruel» are close in meaning to unfeeling, but cruel means deliberately causing pain.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice finds some creatures unfeeling, such as the Queen who orders heads cut off.
fact: The opposite of unfeeling is kind, caring or sympathetic.
exercise: «The unfeeling king ignored the crying villagers.» What does unfeeling mean here? | Very happy and cheerful | *Not caring about other people's pain | Tired after a long day | Full of strong feelings
exercise: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad calls the people who lock him up unfeeling. What does this tell you about them? | They have only just arrived in the town | They are very kind to animals | *They do not care that Toad is unhappy | They are sleepy after a long night
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unfeeling? | Cruel | Hard-hearted | Numb | *Kind
test: «After the cold walk, her fingers were unfeeling.» What does unfeeling mean here? | Very angry | *Numb, unable to feel anything | Warm and cosy | Sleepy and tired
test: Which sentence shows someone being unfeeling? | Mum gave the puppy a warm blanket. | They shared their lunch with a new classmate. | *He laughed at the boy who had fallen off his bike and did not help him up. | She sat with her friend until he stopped crying.
exam: Which word means not caring about other people's pain? | Hungry | *Unfeeling | Curious | Joyful
